    "collapsible_content_F6H33a": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_ybJ8te": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes Adira Earth soaps unique?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Our soap bars are crafted using traditional methods dating back thousands of years, featuring sustainably sourced ingredients directly from renowned coastal areas. Each bar is handmade with a blend of olive oil, laurel oil, and water, providing gentle yet effective cleansing for all skin types.</p><p>Our soaps undergo an essential curing process, resting for about nine months in a cool, dry place away from the Mediterranean sun. This curing allows the soap to complete the saponification process while developing its signature fragrance and amber color. This crucial step ensures the quality and gentleness of our soaps, making them perfect for your skin.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_aL3XCY": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are Adira Earth soaps suitable for sensitive skin?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Our Aleppo soaps are made with a simple combination of olive oil and laurel oil and are available in different laurel oil concentrations. Some customers with sensitive skin prefer Aleppo soap as part of their cleansing routine, although everyone's skin is different. If your skin is particularly sensitive, we recommend patch testing first and choosing according to your skin's comfort.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_dVCpDj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long do Adira Earth soap bars last?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Our soap bars are long-lasting and will typically last for several weeks with regular use. To prolong the life of your soap bar, be sure to store it in a dry, well-drained soap dish between uses.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_gWNqzR": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do you offer bath gels in addition to soap bars?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, we have a range of luxurious bath gels infused with natural ingredients to cleanse and nourish the skin. Our bath gels are formulated to leave you feeling refreshed and rejuvenated after every use.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_97HADC": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are your bath care products suitable for all skin types?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Our bath care range is designed to be gentle and effective, making it suitable for all skin types. Whether you have dry, oily, or sensitive skin, you can enjoy the benefits of our nourishing bath products.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wLYDna": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do you offer other bath accessories?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, we offer our sustainably-sourced, high-quality Sisal Double Face loofah, ensuring a natural bath experience. Additionally, we're actively exploring more bath accessories to elevate your bathing routine even further.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_8YDG3L": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Benefits",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Traditional Aleppo soap is valued for its simple formulation and centuries-old soap-making tradition. Olive oil forms the foundation of the soap, while laurel oil gives each bar its distinctive character.</p><p>With <a href=\"/blogs/news/how-to-choose-your-aleppo-soap-adira-earth\" title=\"How to Choose Aleppo Soap: Laurel Oil Percentage Guide | Adira Earth\">different laurel oil concentrations</a> available, you can choose from a milder introduction to Aleppo soap through to a more pronounced high-laurel cleansing experience. Its simple combination of olive oil and laurel oil makes Aleppo soap a beautiful addition to an everyday cleansing ritual.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_WGEwDb": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Quality",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>Ingredients:</strong> Traditional Aleppo soap is crafted using olive oil and laurel berry oil through a time-honoured soapmaking process. The finished soap naturally contains glycerin, while the traditional production process also involves water and an alkali. Always check the product's ingredient list when choosing your Aleppo soap.</p><p><strong>Colour and Scent:</strong> Traditionally aged Aleppo soap often develops a golden-brown exterior while retaining a greenish centre. Its natural, earthy scent comes from the olive and laurel oils used in its production. Colour and scent may vary depending on the ingredients and ageing process.</p><p><strong>Exterior Appearance:</strong> Traditional Aleppo soap often has a rustic, hand-cut appearance with a firm, air-dried texture. Natural variations in shape, colour and finish are part of its traditional character.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_9yEgYy": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Composition",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Traditional Aleppo soap is made through the saponification of olive oil and laurel berry oil, a process that naturally produces glycerin. The soap is then traditionally aged to develop its characteristic texture, colour and finish.</p><p><strong>Available Laurel Oil Percentages</strong></p><p>At Adira Earth, our Aleppo soap bars are available in six laurel oil concentrations: <strong>12%, 16%, 20%, 35%, 40% and 55%</strong>, allowing you to choose according to your skin's needs and personal preferences.</p><p><strong>Choosing Your Aleppo Soap</strong></p><p><strong>12% Laurel Oil:</strong> A gentle introduction to traditional Aleppo soap, suitable for those who prefer a lower laurel oil concentration.</p><p><strong>16% and 20% Laurel Oil:</strong> Balanced options for everyday cleansing, offering a step up in laurel oil concentration.</p><p><strong>35% Laurel Oil:</strong> A mid-to-higher concentration for those who prefer a more pronounced laurel oil presence in their daily cleansing routine.</p><p><strong>40% and 55% Laurel Oil:</strong> Our highest laurel oil concentrations, ideal for those seeking a richer laurel oil formulation. Individual skin responses vary, particularly for sensitive or eczema-prone skin, so we recommend patch testing before regular use.</p><p>Not sure which percentage to choose? Explore our <a href=\"/blogs/news/how-to-choose-your-aleppo-soap-adira-earth\" title=\"How to Choose Aleppo Soap: Laurel Oil Percentage Guide | Adira Earth\"><strong>Aleppo Soap Buying Guide</strong></a> to find the right bar for your daily skincare ritual.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_GjRyMD": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Commitment",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>We are dedicated to eco-friendly practices and against animal exploitation. <br/><br/>Our products are:<br/><br/>Animal-Friendly: No animal testing or animal-derived ingredients. <br/>Free From Harmful Chemicals: No parabens, ethyl alcohol, phenoxyethanol, GMOs, palm oil, petrochemicals, phthalates, micronized titanium dioxide, or lead.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
